,"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a8f5e0e64bcf54140ff67fb499468516b47d5baf29d7c61d66c62c9e75114940","event_uuid":"beb3eb4f-d8a7-4c4f-992c-e3a663237e2f","position":{"commit_sha":"74dce3be2972d933e9e54153ffbbd69ce1ebcd18","position":"1788333324288951163-beb3eb4f-d8a7-4c4f-992c-e3a663237e2f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-258_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"b49fe82a-1778-4290-aefd-33d2684ae335","comments":[],"created_at":1788311532647637380,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c6a98013-89df-41a5-8eec-1166005c3957","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e997-e818-a702-4620"},{"link_uuid":"beb3eb4f-d8a7-4c4f-992c-e3a663237e2f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c34-c3c3-7aa2-4166"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe second half of the isolation class (R2S1 category f): shared mutable state across concurrent writers. The exemplar is the completion-verdict cache fixed instance-by-instance in `89981d8e` — two concurrent closes derived the same `<criterion-hash>.tmp` pathname, the first `os.replace` consumed the shared temp, the second raised `FileNotFoundError`, and a best-effort `except Exception` swallowed it, so the loser silently returned 0. The class is \"a process-derived or content-derived name shared across concurrent contexts\"; instances keep recurring because each fix is local.\n\n**A shared helper already exists.** `src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py::atomic_write` (118 LOC, stdlib-only leaf, ~50 call sites) already implements exactly the exemplar's fix — `mkstemp` in the target directory, write, `chmod`, `os.replace`, `unlink` on any exception. Its own module docstring names `rebar.toml` among the sites it was meant to consolidate, yet that site still hand-rolls. So this story is a **conversion of the remaining hazard sites onto the existing helper**, not the authoring of a new one, and it deliberately adds no new module. (The ticket's original guess of `src/rebar/llm/completion_cache.py` and a new `_store/unique_write.py` were both wrong: the real exemplar is `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_verdict_cache.py`.)\n\n## Approach\n\n**Step 1 — the audit is already done and is a deliverable.** An enumeration of cache/temp write sites in `src/rebar` classified every site as ALREADY-UNIQUE, SHARED-NAME-HAZARD, or ROOT-UNKEYED-CACHE. Result: ~30 already-unique sites (using `atomic_write`, `mkstemp`, `NamedTemporaryFile`, `mkdtemp`, or uuid4 naming), **six shared-name hazards**, and — after auditing every module-level cache and `lru_cache` — **zero root-unkeyed caches**: all are keyed by absolute path, repo root, or a stat token, and the two store-state `lru_cache`s are explicitly repo-root + overlay-signature keyed. That negative result is reported, not silently dropped.\n\nThe six hazards:\n\n| site | derivation | atomic today |\n|---|---|---|\n| `review_bot/reconcile.py:177` `_write_cursor` | `p.with_suffix(\".tmp\")` — shared temp; swallows `OSError` | replace, shared temp |\n| `_config_writer.py:279` | `target.name + \".tmp\"` | replace, shared temp |\n| `_cli/__init__.py:253` | `target.name + \".tmp\"` | replace, shared temp |\n| `_opcert_signing.py:77` | `f\"{pub}.{os.getpid()}.tmp\"` — pid-derived, so it collides across THREADS in the threaded MCP server | replace, shared temp |\n| `_snapshot/janitor.py:300` | `f\"{sha}.integrity\"` written directly | **none** — torn read possible |\n| `llm/workflow/completion_banking.py:507` | `self._path(id).write_text(...)` | **none** — run-scoped dir limits collision, torn-read window remains |\n\n**Step 2 — convert.** Each site calls `fsutil.atomic_write`; sites that are deliberately best-effort keep their own `try/except` around the call, which is the contract `atomic_write`'s docstring already states. No site is left deriving its temp name solely from a content or criterion hash.\n\n**Step 3 — regress.** One concurrency test in the shape the exemplar's own regression already established at `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_verdict_cache.py:487`: a `threading.Barrier(2)` with `monkeypatch.setattr` on the module's own `os.replace`, gating only the target write, two threads, asserting both writers' effects land and no `*.tmp` residue remains. This reuses the established in-repo pattern for this exact defect class rather than inventing a harness. The store-level suites are the wrong shape here and are deliberately not used: `tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py` is a subprocess storm and `tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py` covers sync/freshness contention, neither providing a two-writer barrier at a single file write.\n\nFor `review_bot/reconcile.py` specifically the write swallows `OSError` and returns `None`, so the assertion must be on file CONTENT, not on a return value.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: a site table classifying every cache/temp write site found, with `file:line` and verdict, is committed in the change description, including the explicit negative result that no root-unkeyed cache was found.\n- [ ] AC2: all six shared-name-hazard sites call `fsutil.atomic_write`, and no site derives a temp name solely from a content/criterion hash or a fixed literal. Verified by `grep -rn 'with_suffix(.*tmp\\|+ \\\".tmp\\\"\\|getpid()}.tmp' src/rebar` returning no write-path hits.\n- [ ] AC3: a two-writer concurrency regression test passes against the converted code and fails RED against the old shared-name pattern. Verified by `pytest tests/unit/test_unique_cache_writes.py -v`, and by the mutation check restoring a shared-temp derivation and observing the test go red.\n- [ ] AC4: the two no-temp sites (`janitor.py:300`, `completion_banking.py:507`) become atomic, closing the torn-read window. Verified by the same suite asserting a reader never observes a partial file.\n- [ ] AC5: no new module or helper is added — the change consumes the existing `fsutil.atomic_write`. Verified by the diff touching no new file under `src/rebar/_store/`.\n- [ ] AC6: `atomic_write`'s role as the single house helper for this class is documented where the isolation helpers are documented.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_unique_cache_writes.py -v` — the two-writer barrier regression (AC3) and the torn-read assertions for the two previously non-atomic sites (AC4).\n- `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_verdict_cache.py -v` — the exemplar's existing concurrency regression still passes, proving the conversion did not regress the already-fixed site.\n- `grep -rn 'with_suffix(.*tmp\\|+ \\\".tmp\\\"\\|getpid()}.tmp' src/rebar` — no remaining shared-name temp derivations on a write path (AC2).\n- `make lint && make typecheck && make test` — the house gates, including the complexity ratchet over the touched modules.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py`, `src/rebar/_config_writer.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py`, `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py`, `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py`, `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py` (the six hazard sites converted to `fsutil.atomic_write`)\n- `tests/unit/test_unique_cache_writes.py` (new; two-writer barrier regression + torn-read assertions)\n- `docs/` (note `atomic_write` as the house helper for this class, beside the isolation helpers)","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py","reason":"convert _write_cursor shared temp to fsutil.atomic_write"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_writer.py","reason":"convert shared-name temp to fsutil.atomic_write"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"convert suggest-mapping config write to fsutil.atomic_write"},{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py","reason":"pid-derived temp name collides across threads; convert to fsutil.atomic_write"},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py","reason":"non-atomic integrity write; close torn-read window"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py","reason":"non-atomic bank record write; close torn-read window"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_unique_cache_writes.py","reason":"two-writer barrier regression + torn-read assertions"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","87cb-7121-a3b6-4606"],["relates_to","9c34-c3c3-7aa2-4166"],["relates_to","e997-e818-a702-4620"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"87cb-7121-a3b6-4606","parent_status_uuid":"116f5fb5-95d8-4275-8caf-9f545cc5383e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b0ac-3c0f-3f64-4344","ticket_type":"story","title":"Key process-local caches and shared temp artifacts by isolation root","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8fe6034e-2e49-4f4b-8816-7bbc7867a3cb","ef93d98d-9cb6-436f-8365-634ea7d009d2","b0813320-a402-44f1-bb4f-6f3726809607","6cb9b6ad-3884-4af7-aaa0-1c9d61e6e6d4","8304cbc4-2df7-4ede-b049-a1f612932377","116f5fb5-95d8-4275-8caf-9f545cc5383e","0bdb234a-006c-4d20-bb8f-b8ebe43d58d0","c6a98013-89df-41a5-8eec-1166005c3957","ef775a36-b73a-431d-9a69-74b69d4ac834","e9c2374b-dc4d-4342-9700-1bdedd0e8e13","beb3eb4f-d8a7-4c4f-992c-e3a663237e2f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788336566718688001,"uuid":"0a4faf3d-9c57-4dda-b7c5-a425cc72a4fa"}